{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 8,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Set",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the trumpet to thy mouth. ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "He shall come",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as an eagle against the house of the LORD, because they have transgressed my covenant, and trespassed against my law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Israel shall cry to me, My God, we know thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Israel hath cast off ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the thing that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good: the enemy shall pursue him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have set up kings, but not by me: they have made princes, and I knew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not: of their silver and their gold have they made for themselves idols, that they may be cut off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy calf, O Samaria, hath cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " off; my anger is kindled against them: how long ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will it be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ere they attain to innocence?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For from Israel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it also: the workman made it; therefore it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not God: but the calf of Samaria shall be broken in pieces.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they have sown the wind, and they shall reap the whirlwind: it hath no stalk: the bud shall yield no meal: if it shall yield, the strangers shall swallow it up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Israel is swallowed up: now shall they be among the Gentiles as a vessel in which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no pleasure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they have gone up to Assyria, a wild ass alone by himself: Ephraim hath hired lovers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, though they have hired among the nations, now will I gather them, and they shall sorrow a little for the burden of the king of princes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because Ephraim hath made many altars to sin, altars shall be to him to sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have written to him the great things of my law, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they were counted as a strange thing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They sacrifice flesh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sacrifices of my offerings, and eat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD accepteth them not; now will he remember their iniquity, and visit their sins: they shall return to Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.8.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.8.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Israel hath forgotten his Maker, and buildeth temples; and Judah hath multiplied fortified cities: but I will send a fire upon his cities, and it shall devour the palaces thereof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
